# Never stop halfway

The owner does not read code. Leftover agent work stays broken forever.

Finish the **named outcome** of the job you were given. Then stop. Do not start the next job.

“Do this one job and stop” means finish that job completely. It is not permission to ship a
half-finished version.

These are not done:

- A “source candidate,” “revise,” or “gates open” result when the brief said that picture must not ship
- Reviews that listed defects, with those defects still visible
- Ending a turn to wait, ask, or continue later
- Hashes, gate names, or ledgers instead of the player-facing thing

If genuinely blocked, say **not done** in one plain sentence. A quality miss is not a blocker — keep working.

Full rule: `CLAUDE.md`.
